like there are people who do this diet

2896
01:54:39.030 --> 01:54:42.190
and they say that it improves their autoimmune disease.

2897
01:54:42.190 --> 01:54:44.310
I attribute that to the fact

2898
01:54:44.310 --> 01:54:47.300
that you have removed ultra processed foods from your diet.

2899
01:54:47.300 --> 01:54:48.540
That's what I think you've done.

2900
01:54:48.540 --> 01:54:51.370
I don't think it's that the meat heals,

2901
01:54:51.370 --> 01:54:52.680
I think it's that you've withdrawn

2902
01:54:52.680 --> 01:54:54.730
these ultra processed foods that were negatively effective.

2903
01:54:54.730 --> 01:54:55.563
It's interesting.

2904
01:54:55.563 --> 01:54:58.110
'Cause that's the same argument that's used,

2905
01:54:58.110 --> 01:54:59.730
you know, with respect to plant-based.

2906
01:54:59.730 --> 01:55:02.010
Like, that's why you feel better eating plant-based

2907
01:55:02.010 --> 01:55:04.180
'cause you've removed all the process stuff.

2908
01:55:04.180 --> 01:55:06.730
Well, and I think that that's a theme

2909
01:55:06.730 --> 01:55:09.050
that brings together all these dietary tribes

2910
01:55:09.050 --> 01:55:11.450
where we may be casting stones at one another.

2911
01:55:11.450 --> 01:55:13.510
But that is one thing that we will all agree on,

2912
01:55:13.510 --> 01:55:15.880
which I think, you know, at least we have that.

2913
01:55:15.880 --> 01:55:16.713
Right.

2914
01:55:16.713 --> 01:55:18.090
So, but the problem is, Rich,

2915
01:55:18.090 --> 01:55:20.970
that you withdraw these foods, right?

2916
01:55:20.970 --> 01:55:23.070
And you say, "Well, my gut is healed."

2917
01:55:23.070 --> 01:55:25.270
Your gut is not healed

2918
01:55:25.270 --> 01:55:28.010
because you have the absence of discomfort.

2919
01:55:28.010 --> 01:55:29.450
Your gut is healed when you're able

2920
01:55:29.450 --> 01:55:31.090
to actually tolerate those foods

2921
01:55:32.050 --> 01:55:36.120
and a person who withdraws these foods on a carnivore diet,

2922
01:55:36.120 --> 01:55:37.760
if they reintroduce these foods,

2923
01:55:37.760 --> 01:55:38.740
their food intolerances

2924
01:55:38.740 --> 01:55:41.150
are even worse than when they started.

2925
01:55:41.150 --> 01:55:42.810
And so you're not actually healing the gut.

2926
01:55:42.810 --> 01:55:44.190
If anything I believe that you're making

2927
01:55:44.190 --> 01:55:47.240
your gut health worse in the process of doing this.

2928
01:55:47.240 --> 01:55:48.840
You're completely devoid of fiber,

2929
01:55:48.840 --> 01:55:52.267
which is the key from my perspective for optimal gut health,

2930
01:55:52.267 --> 01:55:55.260
and at the same time you're cranking up the saturated fat

2931
01:55:55.260 --> 01:55:58.500
to a level that's very deeply disturbing.

2932
01:55:58.500 --> 01:55:59.930
And that this ultimately,

2933
01:55:59.930 --> 01:56:02.340
like saturated fat has negative effects

2934
01:56:02.340 --> 01:56:03.743
on the gut microbiome.

2935
01:56:04.610 --> 01:56:08.040
Now going beyond gut health,

2936
01:56:08.040 --> 01:56:11.470
talking about other health outcomes, for example.

2937
01:56:11.470 --> 01:56:13.620
People will say, well, I cured by diabetes.

2938
01:56:13.620 --> 01:56:14.816
You did not cure your diabetes

2939
01:56:14.816 --> 01:56:16.860
because if you have a piece of fruit

2940
01:56:16.860 --> 01:56:19.820
your blood sugar is gonna be off the charts.

2941
01:56:19.820 --> 01:56:21.820
Saturated fat actually contributes

2942
01:56:21.820 --> 01:56:25.450
to insulin resistance through a process called lipotoxicity.

2943
01:56:25.450 --> 01:56:28.820
Anyone can look up research studies on lipotoxicity.

2944
01:56:28.820 --> 01:56:29.790
And what you're gonna find

2945
01:56:29.790 --> 01:56:33.530
is that it's not that the fruit is the problem,

2946
01:56:33.530 --> 01:56:36.440
it's that the saturated fat is the problem,

2947
01:56:36.440 --> 01:56:38.880
and then it's affecting your insulin resistance,

2948
01:56:38.880 --> 01:56:39.990
and then you spike your blood sugar

2949
01:56:39.990 --> 01:56:42.090
after you eat the piece of fruit, right?

2950
01:56:42.090 --> 01:56:44.330
So this is what happens in this particular case.

2951
01:56:44.330 --> 01:56:46.180
They say, "Oh, well I cured my diabetes."

2952
01:56:46.180 --> 01:56:49.120
No, 'cause you're not capable of eating normal food

2953
01:56:49.120 --> 01:56:51.220
without your blood sugar going off the charts

2954
01:56:51.220 --> 01:56:53.420
because your diet has made you insulin resistant.

2955
01:56:53.420 --> 01:56:54.253
Right.

2956
01:56:54.253 --> 01:56:56.925
Your insulin resistant resistance is still there,

2957
01:56:56.925 --> 01:56:58.810
it's just not being tested.

2958
01:56:58.810 --> 01:57:00.700
So you think that it's resolved.

2959
01:57:00.700 --> 01:57:01.533
Exactly.

2960
01:57:01.533 --> 01:57:04.860
So this is the functional equivalent of like,

2961
01:57:04.860 --> 01:57:07.150
if you are out running one day

2962
01:57:07.150 --> 01:57:08.560
and you're running on a trail

2963
01:57:08.560 --> 01:57:11.610
and you step funny on a route of a tree

2964
01:57:11.610 --> 01:57:14.040
and you twist your knee, right?

2965
01:57:14.040 --> 01:57:16.030
And it's like, okay, so Rich,

2966
01:57:16.030 --> 01:57:19.270
you could stop walking permanently

2967
01:57:20.747 --> 01:57:22.847
and you will never feel pain in your knee,

2968
01:57:23.940 --> 01:57:28.940
but your legs atrophy, and now you're sedentary

2969
01:57:29.460 --> 01:57:31.807
and your metabolism gets outta whack and you gain weight

2970
01:57:31.807 --> 01:57:33.150
and your blood pressure goes up

2971
01:57:33.150 --> 01:57:34.430
and so does your cholesterol,

2972
01:57:34.430 --> 01:57:36.190
and now you have cardiac risk factors

2973
01:57:36.190 --> 01:57:37.023
and you give enough time

2974
01:57:37.023 --> 01:57:39.530
and this is how you get to coronary artery disease, right?

2975
01:57:39.530 --> 01:57:42.620
So the avoidance is not the solution.

2976
01:57:42.620 --> 01:57:45.000
You twist your knee when you're out running on the trail,

2977
01:57:45.000 --> 01:57:50.000
and the solution is to heal the knee, to restore function.

2978
01:57:50.460 --> 01:57:51.840
And that's working through a process

2979
01:57:51.840 --> 01:57:53.950
like perhaps with a physical therapist,

2980
01:57:53.950 --> 01:57:55.340
where you work through this process

2981
01:57:55.340 --> 01:57:58.560
with this physical therapist restoring function to the knee.

2982
01:57:58.560 --> 01:58:01.260
And yes, there may be some discomfort in that process.

2983
01:58:02.210 --> 01:58:03.980
But when you emerge on the other side,

2984
01:58:03.980 --> 01:58:07.110
you're running again and you're as strong as ever.

2985
01:58:07.110 --> 01:58:07.943
Right.

2986
01:58:07.943 --> 01:58:08.776
And this is the issue.

2987
01:58:08.776 --> 01:58:10.150
Is that the avoidance that we see,

2988
01:58:10.150 --> 01:58:12.200
whether it's in terms of the gut

2989
01:58:12.200 --> 01:58:14.200
or in terms of your blood glucose,

2990
01:58:14.200 --> 01:58:16.670
is not actually making you stronger,

2991
01:58:16.670 --> 01:58:19.440
it's making you weaker, but because you're avoiding it,

2992
01:58:19.440 --> 01:58:21.170
you can pretend that you have fixed

2993
01:58:21.170 --> 01:58:23.993
your blood glucose level because it comes down.

2994
01:58:24.860 --> 01:58:26.180
I think the last thing I wanna say real quick

2995
01:58:26.180 --> 01:58:30.040
about this is that because, about the carnivore diet,

2996
01:58:30.040 --> 01:58:35.040
is that because the consumption of saturated is so high,

2997
01:58:36.540 --> 01:58:40.193
saturated fat drives up LDL cholesterol.

2998
01:58:41.210 --> 01:58:45.280
LDL Cholesterol is a widely accepted risk factor

2999
01:58:45.280 --> 01:58:47.610
for coronary artery disease.

3000
01:58:47.610 --> 01:58:51.117
This goes beyond epidemiology studies where we say,

3001
01:58:51.117 --> 01:58:53.530
"Oh, a person with higher cholesterol,

3002
01:58:53.530 --> 01:58:57.100
LDL cholesterol has higher risk of coronary artery disease.

3003
01:58:57.100 --> 01:58:58.133
Yes, that is true.

3004
01:58:59.400 --> 01:59:04.050
But then we have multiple different drug interventions

3005
01:59:04.050 --> 01:59:06.070
of different classes that work

3006
01:59:06.070 --> 01:59:10.060
in different ways to lower LDL cholesterol

3007
01:59:10.060 --> 01:59:12.120
and in these clinical trials

3008
01:59:12.120 --> 01:59:15.240
people are less likely to have a heart attack

3009
01:59:15.240 --> 01:59:17.023
and die of heart disease.

3010
01:59:18.100 --> 01:59:21.550
Any person who promotes a carnivore diet

3011
01:59:21.550 --> 01:59:23.450
and tells you that the LDL cholesterol

3012
01:59:23.450 --> 01:59:27.150
is not relevant is causing harm.

3013
01:59:27.150 --> 01:59:28.200
Well, that's the party line.

3014
01:59:28.200 --> 01:59:30.037
They're very dismissive of this and say,

3015
01:59:30.037 --> 01:59:32.227
"Don't worry about your elevated LDL.

3016
01:59:32.227 --> 01:59:34.250
"It's not what you think it is."

3017
01:59:34.250 --> 01:59:35.590
Do you wanna be the Guinea pig

3018
01:59:35.590 --> 01:59:39.750
who has the crushing myocardial infarction at the age of 48,

3019
01:59:39.750 --> 01:59:42.270
and you never get to see your grandkids?

3020
01:59:42.270 --> 01:59:43.340
Do you wanna be that Guinea pig?

3021
01:59:43.340 --> 01:59:44.250
We don't have that data,

3022
01:59:44.250 --> 01:59:45.770
but what we do know is this,

3023
01:59:45.770 --> 01:59:48.940
and an LDL cholesterol that's off the charts,

3024
01:59:48.940 --> 01:59:51.240
all I can say is, show me a cardiologist

3025
01:59:51.240 --> 01:59:52.260
that's willing to come in here

3026
01:59:52.260 --> 01:59:53.760
and tell you that that's okay.

3027
01:59:56.535 --> 01:59:59.240
You don't have to convince me, you know.

3028
01:59:59.240 --> 02:00:03.460
It would be interesting to do a long term study

3029
02:00:03.460 --> 02:00:06.480
on the microbiome of people

3030
02:00:06.480 --> 02:00:09.997
who have persisted on a current carnivore diet.

3031
02:00:09.997 --> 02:00:10.930
Yeah, or a keto diet.
We'd see with that.

3032
02:00:10.930 --> 02:00:11.763
Yeah, exactly.

3033
02:00:11.763 --> 02:00:12.798
I would be very interested to see it.

3034
02:00:12.798 --> 02:00:13.631
Yeah.

3035
02:00:13.631 --> 02:00:14.464
Like I'm very open to these things.

3036
02:00:14.464 --> 02:00:17.090
I'm not here to attack people or be a zealot about this.

3037
02:00:17.090 --> 02:00:18.660
Like again, I'm here to tell people

3038
02:00:18.660 --> 02:00:21.010
that there are many different forms of a healthy diet,

3039
02:00:21.010 --> 02:00:22.470
but based upon everything that I've seen,

3040
02:00:22.470 --> 02:00:24.190
these are plant predominant diets.

3041
02:00:24.190 --> 02:00:28.130
And so I think that all of us, if you are 10% plant-based,

3042
02:00:28.130 --> 02:00:32.150
that is more than I was and you just take it one day,

3043
02:00:32.150 --> 02:00:34.280
one meal at a time,

3044
02:00:34.280 --> 02:00:35.290
moving in this direction

3045
02:00:35.290 --> 02:00:36.980
and don't put much pressure on yourself.

3046
02:00:36.980 --> 02:00:38.010
Yeah.

3047
02:00:38.010 --> 02:00:41.350
You mentioned food intolerances and allergies.

3048
02:00:41.350 --> 02:00:42.320
I want to get into that.

3049
02:00:42.320 --> 02:00:44.270
But before I do, I think just to put a cap

3050
02:00:44.270 --> 02:00:46.723
on this portion of the discussion,

3051
02:00:47.590 --> 02:00:50.810
I wanted to remark on how interesting

3052
02:00:50.810 --> 02:00:54.626
and cool it's been to see the popularity

3053
02:00:54.626 --> 02:00:59.060
of a plant-based or plant predominant plant-centric approach

3054
02:00:59.060 --> 02:01:04.060
to diet is becoming in certain circles

3055
02:01:05.940 --> 02:01:08.900
that have been traditionally resistant to this idea.

3056
02:01:08.900 --> 02:01:11.589
And by that I mean the kind of biohacking

3057
02:01:11.589 --> 02:01:16.180
or longevity interested or obsessed space,

3058
02:01:16.180 --> 02:01:18.940
which has typically been populated with people

3059
02:01:18.940 --> 02:01:21.070
who are more interested in a low carb approach

3060
02:01:21.070 --> 02:01:22.180
or a keto approach,

3061
02:01:22.180 --> 02:01:27.180
'cause that's more of a biohacking lens on health.

3062
02:01:27.190 --> 02:01:31.440
But you know, for example, I mentioned Justin Sonnenburg

3063
02:01:31.440 --> 02:01:34.610
recently being on Andrew Huberman and he was very clear.

3064
02:01:34.610 --> 02:01:36.350
Like if you wanna, you know,

3065
02:01:36.350 --> 02:01:38.722
basically take an insurance policy out on longevity

3066
02:01:38.722 --> 02:01:42.210
and you want your metabolism to operate

3067
02:01:42.210 --> 02:01:46.140
optimally being as plant predominant as possible is key.

3068
02:01:46.140 --> 02:01:49.770
And Andrew is a guy whose audience I would suspect

3069
02:01:49.770 --> 02:01:52.760
is populated with a lot of kind of biohacking

3070
02:01:52.760 --> 02:01:54.417
low-carb keto type of people.

3071
02:01:54.417 --> 02:01:55.250
Sure.

3072
02:01:55.250 --> 02:01:56.747
So I found that to be super interesting.

3073
02:01:56.747 --> 02:01:57.580
Yeah.

3074
02:01:57.580 --> 02:02:00.310
And then in the longevity space you have David Sinclair,

3075
02:02:00.310 --> 02:02:01.820
who's going plant-based,

3076
02:02:01.820 --> 02:02:04.630
he's influenced Peter Diamandis, who was recently here.

3077
02:02:04.630 --> 02:02:05.580
Who is plant-based.

3078
02:02:05.580 --> 02:02:06.930
These are people who are obsessed

3079
02:02:06.930 --> 02:02:09.186
with living as long as possible.

3080
02:02:09.186 --> 02:02:10.019
Yep.

3081
02:02:10.019 --> 02:02:11.770
And that is very much a biohacking thing

3082
02:02:11.770 --> 02:02:15.440
that has Silicon Valley, you know, very focused on this,

3083
02:02:15.440 --> 02:02:18.670
and to the extent that a plant predominant diet

3084
02:02:18.670 --> 02:02:23.070
is contributing to this, you know,

3085
02:02:23.070 --> 02:02:28.070
idea of human health span extension,

3086
02:02:28.180 --> 02:02:30.330
I find to be super interesting.

3087
02:02:30.330 --> 02:02:31.900
We both know to Tom Bilyeu, you,

3088
02:02:31.900 --> 02:02:35.050
I recently was over at his house, I did his show again,

3089
02:02:35.050 --> 02:02:36.270
and one of the reasons he invited

3090
02:02:36.270 --> 02:02:37.660
me back on is he wanted to learn

3091
02:02:37.660 --> 02:02:41.330
more about being plant-based because he too had Peter on,

3092
02:02:41.330 --> 02:02:45.840
and he had David on and he's hearing about how,

3093
02:02:45.840 --> 02:02:46.673
you know,

3094
02:02:46.673 --> 02:02:47.710
moving in a plant-based direction

3095
02:02:47.710 --> 02:02:49.760
is so important in terms of longevity,

3096
02:02:49.760 --> 02:02:51.770
which is something that Tom is really interested in.

3097
02:02:51.770 --> 02:02:52.603
Yep.

3098
02:02:52.603 --> 02:02:53.436
And the fact that, you know,

3099
02:02:53.436 --> 02:02:55.810
people like this who traditionally,

3100
02:02:55.810 --> 02:02:58.100
I don't know if I would characterize them as resistant,

3101
02:02:58.100 --> 02:03:01.390
but just not part of the plant-based

3102
02:03:01.390 --> 02:03:02.976
kind of subculture.

3103
02:03:02.976 --> 02:03:03.809
Yeah.

3104
02:03:03.809 --> 02:03:05.020
Are now thinking about it

3105
02:03:05.020 --> 02:03:08.290
and practicing it in a way that even I don't think

3106
02:03:08.290 --> 02:03:09.330
I would've predicted.

3107
02:03:09.330 --> 02:03:10.163
Yeah.

3108
02:03:10.163 --> 02:03:11.030
Well I think that...

3109
02:03:11.030 --> 02:03:14.300
So first of all, I think that makes me respect

3110
02:03:14.300 --> 02:03:17.480
them so much because that means

3111
02:03:17.480 --> 02:03:20.070
that they haven't just planted their flag

3112
02:03:20.070 --> 02:03:21.630
and standing by their flag,

3113
02:03:21.630 --> 02:03:25.140
which is far too common in our society these days.

3114
02:03:25.140 --> 02:03:28.520
You have to use the brain that exists between your ears.

3115
02:03:28.520 --> 02:03:32.320
You have to continue to evolve and strive to do better.

3116
02:03:32.320 --> 02:03:34.820
And that's a part of having the humility

3117
02:03:34.820 --> 02:03:38.040
to say that what I believe today may change tomorrow.

3118
02:03:38.040 --> 02:03:39.130
Right?

3119
02:03:39.130 --> 02:03:41.590
As opposed to being rigid about your views

3120
02:03:41.590 --> 02:03:44.120
and being unwilling to adapt to new information

3121
02:03:44.120 --> 02:03:45.890
that becomes available to you.

3122
02:03:45.890 --> 02:03:47.900
So it makes me have great respect for these people.

3123
02:03:47.900 --> 02:03:49.840
But now the flip side of this though, Rich,

3124
02:03:49.840 --> 02:03:52.260
is look, I think that's great,

3125
02:03:52.260 --> 02:03:57.050
and I want the most inclusive plant-based tent

3126
02:03:57.050 --> 02:03:58.750
humanly possible.

3127
02:03:58.750 --> 02:04:00.740
I want everyone to feel like they're welcome

3128
02:04:00.740 --> 02:04:01.573
coming into this.

3129
02:04:01.573 --> 02:04:03.970
This is not an elite type of thing.

3130
02:04:03.970 --> 02:04:05.720
And there should not be any holier-than-thou

3131
02:04:05.720 --> 02:04:06.760
that exists in my tent.

3132
02:04:06.760 --> 02:04:08.340
That's for sure.

3133
02:04:08.340 --> 02:04:09.890
But at the end of the day

3134
02:04:09.890 --> 02:04:12.643
if we look at meat consumption in the United States,

3135
02:04:13.570 --> 02:04:15.500
it is not going down.

3136
02:04:15.500 --> 02:04:17.540
Right.
It's going up.

3137
02:04:17.540 --> 02:04:21.010
So as good as I may feel about my book

3138
02:04:21.010 --> 02:04:23.373
going out and touching 200,000 people,

3139
02:04:24.210 --> 02:04:25.760
I have not accomplished my goal

3140
02:04:26.880 --> 02:04:28.640
and we had a lot of work to do.

3141
02:04:28.640 --> 02:04:30.890
Yeah.
Amen that.

3142
02:04:30.890 --> 02:04:32.290
I can't let you go without talking

3143
02:04:32.290 --> 02:04:34.240
about food intolerances and allergies.

3144
02:04:34.240 --> 02:04:36.670
This is something that a lot of people suffer from.

3145
02:04:36.670 --> 02:04:39.550
So me through how you think about this

3146
02:04:39.550 --> 02:04:42.610
and what kind of guidance you can give people

3147
02:04:42.610 --> 02:04:45.440
who are dealing with this type of problem

3148
02:04:45.440 --> 02:04:47.500
that continues to trip them up.

3149
02:04:47.500 --> 02:04:48.333
Okay.

3150
02:04:48.333 --> 02:04:49.700
So let's separate these two things

3151
02:04:49.700 --> 02:04:51.320
because I think that it's important for people

3152
02:04:51.320 --> 02:04:53.910
to understand the difference between these two.

3153
02:04:53.910 --> 02:04:57.640
Food allergies versus food intolerances.

3154
02:04:57.640 --> 02:05:01.120
In both cases, it starts with the consumption of food.

3155
02:05:01.120 --> 02:05:02.770
You put something into your mouth

3156
02:05:02.770 --> 02:05:04.130
and then there's some sort of reaction

3157
02:05:04.130 --> 02:05:06.450
that takes place that follows that.

3158
02:05:06.450 --> 02:05:08.690
But it's different things between these two.

3159
02:05:08.690 --> 02:05:13.580
A food allergy involves the activation of the immune system.

3160
02:05:13.580 --> 02:05:17.993
Your immune system has decided that this food is the enemy.

3161
02:05:18.940 --> 02:05:20.270
Any allergy, I mean,

3162
02:05:20.270 --> 02:05:22.760
literally the definition of the word allergy

3163
02:05:22.760 --> 02:05:24.630
is the activation of the immune system

3164
02:05:24.630 --> 02:05:27.460
in response to some sort of outside stimulus.

3165
02:05:27.460 --> 02:05:30.753
So like asthma is an allergy in our lungs.

3166
02:05:31.810 --> 02:05:35.130
We have seasonal allergies and allergic rhinitis

3167
02:05:35.130 --> 02:05:36.200
in our sinuses,

3168
02:05:36.200 --> 02:05:39.347
and this may be like dander that's causing that.

3169
02:05:39.347 --> 02:05:42.610
And in this case, we're talking about food,

3170
02:05:42.610 --> 02:05:44.280
and there are specific foods

3171
02:05:44.280 --> 02:05:45.941
that have been most clearly associated

3172
02:05:45.941 --> 02:05:48.370
with the development of food allergies.

3173
02:05:48.370 --> 02:05:50.810
About 90% of food allergies can be attributed

3174
02:05:50.810 --> 02:05:52.310
to a limited group.

3175
02:05:52.310 --> 02:05:57.310
That includes dairy, eggs, fish,

3176
02:05:57.750 --> 02:06:02.750
shellfish, soy, wheat, peanuts, nuts, and corn.

3177
02:06:06.220 --> 02:06:07.680
I'm very proud of myself for getting through all that.

3178
02:06:07.680 --> 02:06:08.513
Yeah.

3179
02:06:08.513 --> 02:06:11.080
Why do you distinguish with between peanuts and nuts?

3180
02:06:11.080 --> 02:06:12.990
Peanuts are legumes.

3181
02:06:12.990 --> 02:06:14.050
Peanuts are actually legumes.

3182
02:06:14.050 --> 02:06:14.883
Most people don't realize that.

3183
02:06:14.883 --> 02:06:15.716
It's that right.
So yeah.

3184
02:06:15.716 --> 02:06:17.130
Peanuts are actually closer to a bean

3185
02:06:17.130 --> 02:06:18.140
than they are to a nut, so.

3186
02:06:18.140 --> 02:06:19.644
Wow.

3187
02:06:19.644 --> 02:06:21.990
Why so much peanut allergy out there?

3188
02:06:21.990 --> 02:06:22.823
They're very common.

3189
02:06:22.823 --> 02:06:25.160
And actually there's interesting research

3190
02:06:25.160 --> 02:06:29.100
looking at development of the infant microbiome

3191
02:06:29.100 --> 02:06:33.530
and the belief that food allergies in children

3192
02:06:33.530 --> 02:06:36.380
come from disturbances of the gut microbiome

3193
02:06:36.380 --> 02:06:37.870
Wow.
In these children.

3194
02:06:37.870 --> 02:06:42.210
So anyway, and a food allergy is the activation

3195
02:06:42.210 --> 02:06:43.043
of the immune system

3196
02:06:43.043 --> 02:06:44.230
and it may manifest in a number

3197
02:06:44.230 --> 02:06:46.710
of different ways, that could include GI symptoms.

3198
02:06:46.710 --> 02:06:47.850
Like it could include bloating,

3199
02:06:47.850 --> 02:06:50.840
gas, pain, diarrhea, or constipation,

3200
02:06:50.840 --> 02:06:53.460
but classically we're gonna see other stuff.

3201
02:06:53.460 --> 02:06:57.850
So we're gonna see like hives or a rash

3202
02:06:57.850 --> 02:06:59.500
or the thing that we really worry

3203
02:06:59.500 --> 02:07:02.540
about as doctors is like difficulty breathing,

3204
02:07:02.540 --> 02:07:04.940
labored breathing, throat swelling,

3205
02:07:04.940 --> 02:07:08.440
that's the stuff that we freak out as doctors.

3206
02:07:08.440 --> 02:07:09.500
Now with an allergy,

3207
02:07:09.500 --> 02:07:13.400
one of the important points is that the amount

3208
02:07:13.400 --> 02:07:17.690
that it takes to activate the immune system is very small.

3209
02:07:17.690 --> 02:07:20.270
So if I had a dairy allergy,

3210
02:07:20.270 --> 02:07:23.430
you could potentially put one drop of milk on my tongue

3211
02:07:24.420 --> 02:07:25.253
and that would be enough

3212
02:07:25.253 --> 02:07:27.010
for me to have an allergic reaction.

3213
02:07:28.150 --> 02:07:30.700
Flip side, let's talk about food intolerances.

3214
02:07:30.700 --> 02:07:32.850
They're different and people need to understand

3215
02:07:32.850 --> 02:07:33.683
the difference,

3216
02:07:33.683 --> 02:07:37.310
but food intolerances are always manifested with symptoms.

3217
02:07:37.310 --> 02:07:40.010
You don't have a food intolerance and be symptom free.

3218
02:07:40.920 --> 02:07:43.020
Usually they're digestive symptoms.

3219
02:07:43.020 --> 02:07:48.020
So gas, bloating, abdominal discomfort, cramping, diarrhea,

3220
02:07:48.280 --> 02:07:52.640
constipation, and by definition,

3221
02:07:52.640 --> 02:07:56.320
a food intolerance does not involve activation

3222
02:07:56.320 --> 02:07:57.370
of the immune system.

3223
02:07:58.748 --> 02:07:59.581
So what--

3224
02:07:59.581 --> 02:08:00.414
So if you have hives

3225
02:08:00.414 --> 02:08:04.540
or some kind of other skin manifestation or other condition,

3226
02:08:04.540 --> 02:08:07.035
that's more like an allergy than an intolerance.

3227
02:08:07.035 --> 02:08:07.868
Generally speaking.

3228
02:08:07.868 --> 02:08:08.701
So that is an allergy.

3229
02:08:08.701 --> 02:08:09.534
Generally speaking,

3230
02:08:09.534 --> 02:08:10.500
but we will talk about histamine intolerance

3231
02:08:10.500 --> 02:08:11.990
in a brief, moment here.

3232
02:08:11.990 --> 02:08:12.823
Right.

3233
02:08:12.823 --> 02:08:13.900
And that's an exception to that rule

3234
02:08:13.900 --> 02:08:17.160
that needs to be clarified so that people understand that.

3235
02:08:17.160 --> 02:08:19.980
But a food intolerance is not the immune system.

3236
02:08:19.980 --> 02:08:21.403
So it is not inflammation.

3237
02:08:22.570 --> 02:08:24.833
It is generally sloppy digestion.

3238
02:08:25.700 --> 02:08:27.370
Your gut microbiome,

3239
02:08:27.370 --> 02:08:29.030
which we talked about in the very beginning

3240
02:08:29.030 --> 02:08:32.670
of the show is critical to our digestive process,

3241
02:08:32.670 --> 02:08:34.600
is struggling to keep up with the demands

3242
02:08:34.600 --> 02:08:37.420
of the diet that you're consuming,

3243
02:08:37.420 --> 02:08:38.760
and so when this takes place,

3244
02:08:38.760 --> 02:08:40.830
this is why we get these types of symptoms.

3245
02:08:40.830 --> 02:08:41.980
So we have to separate these two.

3246
02:08:41.980 --> 02:08:44.350
Now, when we test for these things,

3247
02:08:44.350 --> 02:08:47.190
if you were to do food allergy testing

3248
02:08:47.190 --> 02:08:49.020
you would typically go to an allergist

3249
02:08:49.020 --> 02:08:50.380
and there is a couple of different tests

3250
02:08:50.380 --> 02:08:52.260
that they would do, and they would talk you through it.

3251
02:08:52.260 --> 02:08:53.480
You allow a health professional

3252
02:08:53.480 --> 02:08:55.100
to guide you through that process.

3253
02:08:55.100 --> 02:08:57.100
It may involve a skin prick test

3254
02:08:57.100 --> 02:08:58.310
where they basically will inject

3255
02:08:58.310 --> 02:08:59.880
very small amounts of the proteins

3256
02:08:59.880 --> 02:09:01.760
from specific foods underneath your skin

3257
02:09:01.760 --> 02:09:04.700
and they look to see if you get an allergic reaction to it.

3258
02:09:04.700 --> 02:09:05.820
It may involve a blood test,

3259
02:09:05.820 --> 02:09:07.330
where they look at antibody levels,

3260
02:09:07.330 --> 02:09:11.640
specifically IgE antibody levels to see what's going on.

3261
02:09:11.640 --> 02:09:13.910
These tests are not perfect,

3262
02:09:13.910 --> 02:09:16.670
but in the hands of a trained health professional

3263
02:09:16.670 --> 02:09:20.350
they can guide you towards figuring out what the problem is.

3264
02:09:20.350 --> 02:09:22.350
But on the flip side, food intolerances,

3265
02:09:23.330 --> 02:09:25.980
there is poop tests, there is blood tests,

3266
02:09:25.980 --> 02:09:28.340
there is antibody tests, there is saliva tests,

3267
02:09:28.340 --> 02:09:30.330
there is hair tests.

3268
02:09:30.330 --> 02:09:32.280
And none of them have ever been proven.

3269
02:09:33.370 --> 02:09:37.210
And because of that they can create confusion

3270
02:09:37.210 --> 02:09:38.770
and you can receive information

3271
02:09:38.770 --> 02:09:41.150
that makes you not really know what you're supposed to do.

3272
02:09:41.150 --> 02:09:41.983
Right.

3273
02:09:41.983 --> 02:09:44.010
So I've seen a bazillion patients, Rich,

3274
02:09:44.010 --> 02:09:47.250
who their food intolerance tests

3275
02:09:47.250 --> 02:09:50.690
that they ordered off the internet and they did at home,

3276
02:09:50.690 --> 02:09:54.410
it says, "You have a food intolerance to these foods."

3277
02:09:54.410 --> 02:09:56.067
And I say, "Well, do you get any symptoms?"

3278
02:09:56.067 --> 02:09:58.970
They go, "No, I never get any symptoms with those foods."

3279
02:09:58.970 --> 02:10:00.630
You don't have a food intolerance

3280
02:10:00.630 --> 02:10:01.560
and we didn't need the test.

3281
02:10:01.560 --> 02:10:05.250
So what is contributing to that test result?

3282
02:10:05.250 --> 02:10:07.020
Well, many, so it depends on which test you're doing,

3283
02:10:07.020 --> 02:10:09.811
but in many cases it's the IgG antibody

3284
02:10:09.811 --> 02:10:11.230
that they're looking at.

3285
02:10:11.230 --> 02:10:14.450
And IgG is basically the immune system

3286
02:10:14.450 --> 02:10:17.083
being shaped by something that it gets exposed to.

3287
02:10:18.070 --> 02:10:22.390
So quite simply exposure of the immune system

3288
02:10:22.390 --> 02:10:25.330
to regular consumption of certain foods

3289
02:10:25.330 --> 02:10:27.520
could show up on one of these tests.

3290
02:10:27.520 --> 02:10:30.070
And that doesn't mean that it's a food intolerance.

3291
02:10:30.070 --> 02:10:33.460
Again, going back to the definition of a food intolerance.

3292
02:10:33.460 --> 02:10:36.160
A food intolerance does not involve the immune system.

3293
02:10:37.090 --> 02:10:38.910
So if it does not involve the immune system,

3294
02:10:38.910 --> 02:10:41.700
why are we checking IgG antibodies?

3295
02:10:41.700 --> 02:10:43.800
And if it had been proven, I would say it,

3296
02:10:45.461 --> 02:10:47.080
but it has not been proven.

3297
02:10:47.080 --> 02:10:49.360
We don't have any clinical study

3298
02:10:49.360 --> 02:10:53.220
that I would describe as powerful enough to validate

3299
02:10:53.220 --> 02:10:54.830
the use of these tools

3300
02:10:54.830 --> 02:10:57.660
and actually guide people towards good results.

3301
02:10:57.660 --> 02:11:00.120
So what do you do if you're the patient,

3302
02:11:00.120 --> 02:11:03.420
like that's confusing, what am I supposed to do?

3303
02:11:03.420 --> 02:11:06.930
The answer is this, you need a methodology,

3304
02:11:06.930 --> 02:11:08.700
you need a stepwise approach

3305
02:11:08.700 --> 02:11:10.700
that allows you to have information

3306
02:11:10.700 --> 02:11:12.520
that you can wean on with confidence

3307
02:11:12.520 --> 02:11:13.980
and know that you're making the right choice

3308
02:11:13.980 --> 02:11:16.112
with your dietary pattern.

3309
02:11:16.112 --> 02:11:19.230
And that ultimately is what led me to create

3310
02:11:19.230 --> 02:11:22.300
what I call the growth strategy,

3311
02:11:22.300 --> 02:11:23.490
and you'll find this in my new book

3312
02:11:23.490 --> 02:11:25.590
the "Fiber Fields Cookbook".

3313
02:11:25.590 --> 02:11:29.560
So now growth is a very big word in my community

3314
02:11:29.560 --> 02:11:33.300
because I talked about in "Fiber Fields" the growth mindset,

3315
02:11:33.300 --> 02:11:36.250
which came from Carol Dweck, she wrote a book about it.

3316
02:11:36.250 --> 02:11:37.370
Right.

3317
02:11:37.370 --> 02:11:41.330
And so the growth mindset is about ignoring,

3318
02:11:41.330 --> 02:11:43.920
like winning versus losing,

3319
02:11:43.920 --> 02:11:47.510
and instead is about valuing the challenge

3320
02:11:47.510 --> 02:11:49.670
and valuing the process

3321
02:11:49.670 --> 02:11:52.850
and enjoying and celebrating progress

3322
02:11:52.850 --> 02:11:54.603
and letting go of perfection.

3323
02:11:56.530 --> 02:11:59.510
In this case, I'm not talking about the word growth.

3324
02:11:59.510 --> 02:12:01.330
I'm instead using this as an acronym

3325
02:12:02.500 --> 02:12:04.420
to describe the stepwise approach

3326
02:12:04.420 --> 02:12:06.710
that I take to food intolerances

3327
02:12:06.710 --> 02:12:11.710
with my patients to identify and ultimately heal them.

3328
02:12:13.440 --> 02:12:16.903
So the first step is G, G stands for Genesis.

3329
02:12:17.830 --> 02:12:20.440
What is the root of our problem?

3330
02:12:20.440 --> 02:12:22.290
So as a medical doctor

3331
02:12:22.290 --> 02:12:25.370
the first question is, what am I treating?

3332
02:12:25.370 --> 02:12:26.910
Because if I start delivering treatments

3333
02:12:26.910 --> 02:12:27.743
and I don't even know what I'm treating,

3334
02:12:27.743 --> 02:12:28.576
then what am I doing?

3335
02:12:28.576 --> 02:12:30.080
Am I just throwing mud up against the wall

3336
02:12:30.080 --> 02:12:31.960
and hoping something sticks?

3337
02:12:31.960 --> 02:12:33.590
Like at the end of the day

3338
02:12:33.590 --> 02:12:36.660
we are empowered when we know

3339
02:12:36.660 --> 02:12:38.370
and have the right information to know

3340
02:12:38.370 --> 02:12:40.123
exactly what we're going after.

3341
02:12:41.040 --> 02:12:42.283
You have to start there.

3342
02:12:43.830 --> 02:12:45.033
In my book, I introduce something

3343
02:12:45.033 --> 02:12:47.880
called the big three of food sensitivity.

3344
02:12:47.880 --> 02:12:50.220
And these are not the three things

3345
02:12:50.220 --> 02:12:54.010
that are the most common causes of food intolerances,

3346
02:12:54.010 --> 02:12:55.770
but what they are are the three things

3347
02:12:55.770 --> 02:12:58.700
that I as a gastroenterologist as I ponder

3348
02:12:58.700 --> 02:13:01.403
what is the root cause of my patient's problems,

3349
02:13:02.370 --> 02:13:05.640
I wanna make sure that these three things are not present.

3350
02:13:05.640 --> 02:13:09.570
So they are constipation, celiac disease,

3351
02:13:09.570 --> 02:13:10.970
and gallbladder dysfunction.

3352
02:13:11.850 --> 02:13:13.570
There is a process that I go through,

3353
02:13:13.570 --> 02:13:15.040
every single patient that comes in and says,

3354
02:13:15.040 --> 02:13:17.330
I'm having problem with food, Dr. B,

3355
02:13:17.330 --> 02:13:18.490
this is what I'm thinking about.

3356
02:13:18.490 --> 02:13:19.460
These three things,

3357
02:13:19.460 --> 02:13:23.363
because if they are there I can fix them,

3358
02:13:24.200 --> 02:13:26.400
and when I fix them most of the time

3359
02:13:26.400 --> 02:13:29.330
the food intolerances go away entirely,

3360
02:13:29.330 --> 02:13:30.810
and you save yourself from having to go

3361
02:13:30.810 --> 02:13:33.560
through any sort of process 'cause you're done.

3362
02:13:33.560 --> 02:13:34.393
You're good.

3363
02:13:34.393 --> 02:13:35.226
Right.

3364
02:13:35.226 --> 02:13:36.390
The decision tree ends there.

3365
02:13:36.390 --> 02:13:37.750
Exactly.

3366
02:13:37.750 --> 02:13:40.000
So, but once we get past that,

3367
02:13:40.000 --> 02:13:41.520
let's pretend that we identify

3368
02:13:41.520 --> 02:13:42.880
that this is irritable bowel syndrome,

3369
02:13:42.880 --> 02:13:45.310
and we're trying to fix these food intolerances.

3370
02:13:45.310 --> 02:13:46.710
Well, we have to know what foods

3371
02:13:46.710 --> 02:13:48.830
we're actually intolerant of.

3372
02:13:48.830 --> 02:13:49.663
This is where I get back to.

3373
02:13:49.663 --> 02:13:52.220
Like these tests that are commercially available,

3374
02:13:52.220 --> 02:13:55.810
you know, at home, they don't get the job done.

3375
02:13:55.810 --> 02:13:58.811
So we need something that's more reliable than that.

3376
02:13:58.811 --> 02:14:02.300
And the way that we approach this is with R-O-W,

3377
02:14:02.300 --> 02:14:04.170
these three letters in combination

3378
02:14:04.170 --> 02:14:06.040
that are almost like doing a dance together,

3379
02:14:06.040 --> 02:14:07.500
there not one, two, three,

3380
02:14:07.500 --> 02:14:10.170
but instead it's the three of them in a waltz,

3381
02:14:10.170 --> 02:14:13.483
restrict, observe, work it back in.

3382
02:14:15.550 --> 02:14:18.780
When we are observing throughout the entire process,

3383
02:14:18.780 --> 02:14:21.190
keeping notes on how we feel

3384
02:14:21.190 --> 02:14:23.820
and we take the food that we're worried about

3385
02:14:23.820 --> 02:14:28.820
and we withdraw and then reintroduce, off, on,

3386
02:14:29.000 --> 02:14:31.823
off, on, you flip the switch,

3387
02:14:32.830 --> 02:14:36.140
and in doing that, you are creating flows of the current,

3388
02:14:36.140 --> 02:14:37.640
and those flows allow you to determine

3389
02:14:37.640 --> 02:14:39.433
whether or not it's causing issues.

3390
02:14:40.850 --> 02:14:42.700
And you can figure out how much.

3391
02:14:42.700 --> 02:14:44.210
So not only like what foods,

3392
02:14:44.210 --> 02:14:46.710
but also how much of that food is causing trouble.

3393
02:14:47.960 --> 02:14:50.380
So in this process

3394
02:14:50.380 --> 02:14:53.233
you have to first identify what foods you wanna fix.

3395
02:14:54.240 --> 02:14:55.843
But then once you get past that,

3396
02:14:56.740 --> 02:14:58.993
it's time to T, train your gut.

3397
02:15:00.220 --> 02:15:01.280
Train your gut is the process

3398
02:15:01.280 --> 02:15:04.260
that you go through rebuilding

3399
02:15:04.260 --> 02:15:06.573
and restoring function to your gut.

3400
02:15:07.570 --> 02:15:10.710
Your gut can grow stronger.

3401
02:15:10.710 --> 02:15:12.380
You can restore function.

3402
02:15:12.380 --> 02:15:14.200
You are capable of tolerating foods

3403
02:15:14.200 --> 02:15:17.006
that you don't think that you can eat.

3404
02:15:17.006 --> 02:15:18.790
And the way that we do this is the same way

3405
02:15:18.790 --> 02:15:19.993
that we exercise.

3406
02:15:21.050 --> 02:15:23.090
Our body is adaptable.

3407
02:15:23.090 --> 02:15:26.150
Like you become a runner in your forties

3408
02:15:27.420 --> 02:15:31.723
and you progressively ratchet up the distances that you run,

3409
02:15:32.910 --> 02:15:34.443
your legs grow stronger,

3410
02:15:35.280 --> 02:15:38.080
you become more efficient with oxygen,

3411
02:15:38.080 --> 02:15:40.760
your heart chambers grow larger.

3412
02:15:40.760 --> 02:15:43.320
It actually is able to more efficiently squeeze blood,

3413
02:15:43.320 --> 02:15:47.230
so it can slow down and your lungs actually expand

3414
02:15:47.230 --> 02:15:49.270
